## Further Exploration ##
* PR is now running a referral link contest, where customers want to get their
  friends to click on one of these shortened links.  How do we change our system
  to accommodate for this?
  * We have a super famous celebrity who shared a shortened link, and now a
    million customers have clicked on this link at once.  How do you see this
    affecting the database as we try to record the click numbers?
  * Expectation: we can't update the row that quickly - put the clicks in a queue
* We now want our Business Intelligence team to run queries 24/7 against these
  databases in order to get us data on which links are the most effective.  How
  would you change your system to accommodate for this?
  * Expectation: We will add debezium (for RDBMS) in side-car pattern to create a copy of the data just for Business Intelligence to query.
* Along similar lines, how do we clean up links that never get
  visited?
  * Expectation:
  - We can have clean-up service job which can run daily and clean-up the expired-short links.
  - We can also have lazy clean-up where expiration time can be checked from the data of DB or cache when someone tries to access a short link and if it is expired, it is marked expired in DB, invalidated in cache and 404 (resource not found) can be returned to the user.
    401 - unauthorized
    402 - Payment Required
    403 - Forbidden
    404 - resource not found
  - We can also have intelligent clean-up service which can delete only those links which were not used from last one year or two year or so. For that, we will also need last-accessed time in the DB. It is not possible to updated the DB table after every hit. We will need some queue kind of thing and other tables and we can update the main DB once or twice in a day for the last-accessed time.
